  data:  # c28a
    kind: work_item  # c28a
    title: "Edge.create evidence_type default 'ast_call_direct' leaks onto 326 non-call edges (dispatches_to/references/inherits/overrides)"  # c28a
    status: todo_hard  # c28a
    priority: 1  # c28a
    parent:  # c28a
    tags:  # c28a
    - dogfood  # c28a
    - dogfood_tranche_05  # c28a
    isbefore: []  # c28a
    duplicate_of: []  # c28a
    not_duplicate_of: []  # c28a
    pr_ref:  # c28a
    description: "Edge.create's evidence_type parameter defaults to 'ast_call_direct' (ir.py:650; EdgeMeta default ir.py:610). Producers that emit non-call edges without explicitly passing evidence_type inherit this call-specific value, so 326 structurally-non-call edges are stamped as direct function calls on the evidence_type axis: dispatches_to 293 (decorator-dispatch 292 + rust-trait-dispatch-linker 1), references 31 (websocket-linker 30 + solidity 1), inherits 1 (solidity), overrides 1 (solidity). Within a single edge type the axis is inconsistent: dispatches_to splits 293 ast_call_direct vs 326 type_hierarchy for the same relationship. Concrete: inherits Token:contract --(ast_call_direct)--> IToken:interface (a contract→interface inheritance labeled as a direct call); overrides Token.transfer --(ast_call_direct)--> IToken.transfer. Source: solidity.py:395-404 builds the inherits edge via Edge.create() with NO evidence_type kwarg; ir.py:650 default = 'ast_call_direct'. Consequence: a consumer selecting 'all call sites' by filtering edge.meta.evidence_type == 'ast_call_direct' silently pulls in 326 inheritance/override/dispatch/reference edges — wrong call-graph membership for any LLM audit or refactor that trusts the evidence axis."  # c28a
    fields: {}  # c28a
- op: discuss  # c7e6
